                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f9a7e35b-babf-4eff-92c4-9fedc228f47c",
                        "source_entry_id": "547ee5de-7367-31a8-a241-ab9dd92d4fb1",
                        "source_sense_id": "1d43c0f5-e170-30a5-844b-20d1576adc9f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Gouverneuse de province et autres",
                        "target_lang_word": "governoress",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "governoress",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e941b2b-b999-31f9-a3c1-a3e3f63177dd",
                                        "entry_id": "5cbcee51-a254-35d6-b04b-2c742069a071",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A woman employed to educate children in private households."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "nonstandard"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88daa956-53d9-44d4-85ed-d4e90f7f89ac",
                                                "sense_id": "0e941b2b-b999-31f9-a3c1-a3e3f63177dd",
                                                "text": "How are the following nouns improperly formed, and what should they be? viz.—Lifes, knifes, dwarves, mischieves—boxs, churchs, dishs, fishs—enemys, flys, skys, spys—louses, mouses, oxes, pennys—arcanums, datums, erratums, phænomenons—bacheloress, benefactoress, governoress—boys books, girls dolls, childs rattle—diligence sake; Jane’s, Margaret’s, and Isabella’s mother; John’s, Peter’s, and Frank’s books."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8db0a1b0-8041-4473-8a86-6f5dedc54db5",
                                                "sense_id": "0e941b2b-b999-31f9-a3c1-a3e3f63177dd",
                                                "text": "[…] when the hospital established in London for sick governoresses was about to fail for want of proper management, she stepped forward and consented to be placed at its head. Derbyshire and Hampshire were exchanged for the narrow, dreary establishment in Harley street, to which she devoted all her time and fortune. While her friends missed her at assemblies, lectures, concerts, exhibitions and all the entertainments for taste and intellect with which London in its season abounds, she whose powers could have best appreciated these, was sitting beside the bed and soothing the last complaints of some poor, dying, homeless, querulous governess."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca39e37b-61d8-48a4-b1d9-21a92c94128f",
                                                "sense_id": "0e941b2b-b999-31f9-a3c1-a3e3f63177dd",
                                                "text": "It took a firm governoress, boarding school and a finishing school to get rid of the rough edges — and, by her late teens, the young Princess [Alexandra] was emerging as a beautiful and serene woman."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d837d6c5-ed4b-3069-be85-cd28708d2c81",
                                        "entry_id": "5cbcee51-a254-35d6-b04b-2c742069a071",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female governor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3728e58b-55e1-4c55-8a4b-716fdf8c1d11",
                                                "sense_id": "d837d6c5-ed4b-3069-be85-cd28708d2c81",
                                                "text": "I was introduced by Mrs. Onward, the Governoress, to Mrs. Sapient, the Speakeress of the House."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "969532a7-d2f7-498e-96ef-4cbb2cf7c7d4",
                                                "sense_id": "d837d6c5-ed4b-3069-be85-cd28708d2c81",
                                                "text": "Our modern governors (even the current governoress) do not deserve to be belittled as some sort of “gubers.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e4b8538-b517-4315-8074-799ac3eaba6a",
                                                "sense_id": "d837d6c5-ed4b-3069-be85-cd28708d2c81",
                                                "text": "The liberals in control now are just doing what they want. Let’s get things going and separate the states and maybe northern California might like to jump in also. We don’t even have a legal “governoress,” she just thinks she is."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9bc20ff3-fbb4-37d1-b8bd-ce1d352a63ac",
                                        "entry_id": "5cbcee51-a254-35d6-b04b-2c742069a071",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The wife of a governor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "015e38f4-6547-4625-af62-d96e80078eed",
                                                "sense_id": "9bc20ff3-fbb4-37d1-b8bd-ce1d352a63ac",
                                                "text": "Colonel Braddyll, soon after his marriage, was chosen governor of ⸺, in India, and Mrs. Braddyll, as governoress, or governor’s lady, was in the height of her glory."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3468acbb-c1e1-4d99-8a3a-ef9cbe0fd6a2",
                                                "sense_id": "9bc20ff3-fbb4-37d1-b8bd-ce1d352a63ac",
                                                "text": "That reminds me—my old mother in law was here with the Governor and Governoress of Gambia [Southorns] the other day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26f3e6e5-addf-435b-ab19-eb9dbcf7f2a5",
                                                "sense_id": "9bc20ff3-fbb4-37d1-b8bd-ce1d352a63ac",
                                                "text": "“We have strong ties to all,” said Governoress [Adele Khoury] Graham."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "850763e2-69a1-49b5-b394-2ce5965a1b87",
                        "source_entry_id": "547ee5de-7367-31a8-a241-ab9dd92d4fb1",
                        "source_sense_id": "1d43c0f5-e170-30a5-844b-20d1576adc9f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Gouverneuse de province et autres",
                        "target_lang_word": "governor",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "governor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85984639-b289-3c27-b496-c52eb006efc3",
                                        "entry_id": "e1747f0e-9bdb-3d3d-b500-65a1175c4bc2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The chief executive officer of a first-level administrative division of a country."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b34a36f9-8980-4397-bdda-4f85634bc13a",
                                                "sense_id": "85984639-b289-3c27-b496-c52eb006efc3",
                                                "text": "Younger voters are more libertarian in political philosophy than older voters and are credited with the success of libertarian governor Jesse Ventura of Minnesota."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fee4a3d3-5c79-4884-bcc1-2d95e698df74",
                                                "sense_id": "85984639-b289-3c27-b496-c52eb006efc3",
                                                "text": "Top aides and people close to Kamala Harris have divided over whether she should head home to run for California governor in 2026 — and it all comes down to whether they believe she could win the Democratic nomination for president in an expected competitive primary in 2028."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce4e11aa-5e59-4c64-907a-21a73a11b876",
                                                "sense_id": "85984639-b289-3c27-b496-c52eb006efc3",
                                                "text": "But gender is a factor both candidates will navigate in a country that has elected just 51 female state governors in its history."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00fa6075-f930-3214-8d8a-065a9cf4a628",
                                        "entry_id": "e1747f0e-9bdb-3d3d-b500-65a1175c4bc2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A device which regulates or controls some action of a machine through automatic feedback."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04affa7e-fe96-4722-adbd-2f0b7fe1b213",
                                                "sense_id": "00fa6075-f930-3214-8d8a-065a9cf4a628",
                                                "text": "Generator excitation is obtained by a combination of the separately-excited and self-excited fields, and the output is controlled by a resistance in the separate field circuit adjusted by the load regulator under the control of the engine governor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b866fff-8cc1-4dd3-a370-6cd0d5bef059",
                                                "sense_id": "00fa6075-f930-3214-8d8a-065a9cf4a628",
                                                "text": "The turning point came in 1923, says Norton, when 42,000 Cincinnati residents signed a petition for a ballot initiative that would require all cars to have a governor limiting them to 25 miles per hour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0bb7bc73-3b66-3eb2-973c-f93c8f79746e",
                                        "entry_id": "e1747f0e-9bdb-3d3d-b500-65a1175c4bc2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of a decision-making body (such as a committee) for a larger organization or entity (including some public agencies), similar to or equivalent to a board of directors (used especially for banks); a member of the board of governors."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c925c049-cfa5-4885-a5c6-73663ea53d1a",
                                                "sense_id": "0bb7bc73-3b66-3eb2-973c-f93c8f79746e",
                                                "text": "The seven members of the Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System are nominated by the President and confirmed by the Senate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f25ae21c-b9d9-4672-bd91-90ecf9d04e54",
                                                "sense_id": "0bb7bc73-3b66-3eb2-973c-f93c8f79746e",
                                                "text": "Pan Gongsheng, governor of the People’s Bank of China (PBOC) and head of the country’s foreign exchange regulator, chaired a symposium with representatives from foreign companies, including JP Morgan, Tesla (TSLA), HSBC (HSBC), Deutsche Bank (DB), BNP Paribas, Japan’s MUFG Bank, German chemical producer BASF, commodities trader Trafigura and Schneider Electric, according to a statement posted on the websites of the PBOC and the State Administration of Foreign Exchange (SAFE)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "408f6091-1d69-35fa-9c18-a1ab2f422bcb",
                                        "entry_id": "e1747f0e-9bdb-3d3d-b500-65a1175c4bc2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Father."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aea504b5-cbee-4e51-a361-63d4d3187a25",
                                                "sense_id": "408f6091-1d69-35fa-9c18-a1ab2f422bcb",
                                                "text": "\"Say 'father.' We never called him papa; and if one of my brothers had addressed him as 'governor,' as boys do now, I really think he'd have him cut off with a shilling.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c118cc21-83f1-38ce-a28c-434a0cddf7ab",
                                        "entry_id": "e1747f0e-9bdb-3d3d-b500-65a1175c4bc2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Boss; employer; gaffer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "347259e4-c70a-3721-a1ae-34640bed7df9",
                                        "entry_id": "e1747f0e-9bdb-3d3d-b500-65a1175c4bc2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Term of address to a man; guv'nor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dated",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "307d0ee0-dc00-3b71-b076-b83ba5a78b3a",
                                        "entry_id": "e1747f0e-9bdb-3d3d-b500-65a1175c4bc2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A constituent of a phrase that governs another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
